<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Agape love then bids me be</l><l>No more for my own gain;</l><l>For He who loved and rescued me</l><l>Has won my life through pain.</l><l>Can one who’s loved not give his all?</l><l>Divine love paid the cost.</l><l>A life that daily dies, then lives,</l><l>Will ne’er be counted loss.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>To know the riches of His grace,</l><l>Old self I gladly yield;</l><l>Emotion, mind, and will I place</l><l>Within His hands, unsealed.</l><l>A life surrendered wholly, grows,</l><l>His image thus to shine;</l><l>I sense His will and turn aside</l><l>From what is not divine.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>Through consecration’s narrow gate</l><l>I walk and yield each choice;</l><l>In daily steps, both small and great,</l><l>I hear my spirit’s voice.</l><l>Each time His will defeats my own,</l><l>A step ahead is won—</l><l>Each vict’ry o’er my self-bound soul</l><l>Leads ever to the Son.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
